Body:
Work-around for `v1.15.0` using `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` (private Azure OpenAI)

Configure the url as provider-level `api`, not `options.baseURL`. With `options.baseURL`, runtime fails before request auth with `TypeError: "undefined/chat/completions" cannot be parsed as a URL.`

```json
"api": "https://.../openai/deployments/gpt-4.1",
"options": {
  "headers": {
    "api-key": "REDACTED"
  },
  "queryParams": {
    "api-version": "2025-02-01-preview"
  }
}
```

Why it worked (per GPT-5.5):
- `provider.options.baseURL` should work, but it is not reaching  `createOpenAICompatible`.
- `provider.api` becomes `model.api.url`.
- In v1.15.0, `resolveSDK()` falls back from `options.baseURL` to `model.api.url`, then writes that back into `options.baseURL` before constructing the SDK.
